# Always verify production after main

After any change lands on `main` (merge or push), **do not treat the task as done** until the change is confirmed live on https://90books.com.

## Checklist

1. Wait for GitHub Actions **Force production alias** (`.github/workflows/force-booky-prod.yml`) to succeed on the merge commit. If it did not run, trigger `workflow_dispatch`.
2. Fetch the live URLs the change affects (`https://90books.com/`, `/booky`, `/api/booky-words`, `/authors`, etc.) — not only the Vercel Git/preview deploy URL.
3. Assert a **change-specific** string or behavior from the merge appears in the live response.
4. Green Vercel status on the commit alone is **not** proof. If prod is stale, re-run force-alias and re-check until prod matches `main`.
5. Tell the user the live check result (URL, marker checked, pass/fail).
